der_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "303 emits only two events in the window (to 1409 at ~t47k and to 1465 at ~t51-54k). Neither 1409's out-set {960,1490} nor 1465's out-set {2,26,1056,1141,1555,1584,1925,1942} touches 1293's in-neighbours {28,1438,1574}, so no 2-hop time-respecting relay exists. The static connection to 1293 runs through hub 28 (482 events), but the 2-28 edge is directed 28->2 with zero 2->28 events, breaking the only plausible short hub route; the k-hop edge list is undirected and thus cannot support it. Volume and hub popularity therefore explain the apparent link, and no chain of interactions with consecutive gaps <=600 from 303 to 1293 is evidenced."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Endpoints are sparse.** In [33096, 61895], node 303 has only 2 events (both outgoing, to 1409 and 1465), and 1293 has 4 events with in-neighbours {28, 1438, 1574} (steps 02\u201304, 06).\n\n**Timing of 303's activity** (steps 07, 11, 14): its two events land at \u2248[46596,47495] and \u2248[51096,54695]. Since 1465 is completely inactive in [45996,48095] (step 16), the earlier event must be 303\u21921409; the later one is 303\u21921465, inside 1465's activity burst in [51096,55295].\n\n**No short forwarding path exists.** 1409's out-set is {960, 1490} (step 09) and 1465's out-set is {2, 26, 1056, 1141, 1555, 1584, 1925, 1942} (step 10). Neither set intersects 1293's in-neighbour set {28, 1438, 1574} (step 04), so there is no 2-hop time-respecting route.\n\n**Confounder controls.** The apparent \"connection when time is ignored\" runs through hub 28 (482 events, 360 partners \u2014 step 06), which is the only high-volume link to 1293 (step 08). But the candidate hub route 1465\u21922\u219228\u21921293 fails on direction: the 2\u201328 edge is 28\u21922 only, with zero 2\u219228 events (step 13); the k-hop edge listing (step 05) is symmetric and therefore does not establish a usable directed path. So the static reachability is an artefact of hub popularity, not a carrier of influence.\n\nEvery remaining route would need \u22654 hops, each consecutive gap \u2264600, starting from 303's two isolated emissions \u2014 no such chain is evidenced.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_7fc5b54f\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [303, 1293],\n  \"window\": [33096, 61895],\n  \"confidence\": 0.56,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"303 emits only two events in the window (to 1409 at ~t47k and to 1465 at ~t51-54k). Neither 1409's out-set {960,1490} nor 1465's out-set {2,26,1056,1141,1555,1584,1925,1942} touches 1293's in-neighbours {28,1438,1574}, so no 2-hop time-respecting relay exists. The static connection to 1293 runs through hub 28 (482 events), but the 2-28 edge is directed 28->2 with zero 2->28 events, breaking the only plausible short hub route; the k-hop edge list is undirected and thus cannot support it. Volume and hub popularity therefore explain the apparent link, and no chain of interactions with consecutive gaps <=600 from 303 to 1293 is evidenced.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 40865, "total_output_tokens": 7074, "total_tokens": 47939, "total_latency_ms": 92846, "llm_calls": 7, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}